[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4910229558","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-4910229558","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":4910229558,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJKwoNg","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T00:20:24Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T00:20:24Z","body":"Just took a curious look at this, as I was wondering whether a sort was necessary.\r\n\r\nRindbee says that the logic to check for exit of the old shape is happening before the logic to check for entry into the new shape:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/86640#issuecomment-1873712142\r\n\r\nI can logically verify that. The broad phase AABB is creating the exit, while the narrow phase is creating the entry. The broad phase cannot register an entry, because an intersecting AABB does not guarantee that the shapes intersect unless they are purely rectangular. However a non-intersecting AABB does guarantee the shapes have exited, so it should log the exit there cheaply, and not put more load on the narrow phase to confirm the exit.\r\n\r\nI can't see this working any other way without a performance hit. \r\n\r\nI am not so clear on how intersection events get assembled and transmitted, but don't we want to cancel exit and entry events out entirely so that no callback gets triggered at all? Rather than sorting the events?\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4910229558/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4910983546","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-4910983546","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":4910983546,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJLepeg","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T03:00:58Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T03:06:47Z","body":"Ok, so the code looks like it is already doing cancellation of exit and entry events for a single shape. The way the code is written, it looks like it is intentional that an area should receive multiple events for a body if they are happening on different shapes. I think this is confusing and generates additional callbacks, but is no doubt there for a reason, maybe to do with tile maps.\r\n\r\nIf there is a bug this is fixing, then it seems to me like a deeper look is warranted. \r\n\r\nHowever, I can't reproduce the issue from  #86640 (in 4.7). It doesn't seem to be doing what the video is showing. I am not even sure what I am meant to be doing in the game.\r\n\r\nCan you log an issue with a far simpler and clearer reproducible sample? And refer to that in the PR?\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4910983546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4914742859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-4914742859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":4914742859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJPEGSw","user":{"login":"jice-dev","id":3774061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQwNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3774061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/jice-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T12:25:12Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T12:25:12Z","body":"@Schnorg do you mean i must open a new issue and a new PR ? it's pretty confuse and i dont know well all theses processes\r\n\r\ndid you tried rindbee's MRP on the issue ? i reproduced issue with this one and with my own MRP on 4.7 and 4.8.dev, and with sort it was gone.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4914742859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4919909524","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-4919909524","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":4919909524,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJT_clA","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T22:54:00Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T22:54:00Z","body":"> did you tried rindbee's MRP on the issue ? i reproduced issue with this one and with my own MRP on 4.7 and 4.8.dev, and with sort it was gone.\r\n\r\nNo I missed Rindbee's sample (it got confused with other samples). I have since downloaded it though. Apologies for a bit of misunderstanding at first, the issue was outside of my specific experience. \r\n\r\n* I have run the MRP, and I can confirm the issue. \r\n\r\nGodot is triggering Body exit and enter callbacks that it shouldn't because of the ordering of the Body Shape exit and Body Shape enters. The ordering of the body shape enters and exits is not easily fixable IMO (The broadphase triggers the shape exit, while the narrow phase triggers the shape entry). The cancelation code I mentioned is not relevant to this issue. \r\n\r\n* I have built your PR and I can confirm that it fixes the issue with minimal fuss. \r\n* I think it is an important issue for anyone who encounters it.\r\n* I have looked a bit deeper, and this does seem like the place to fix it with a sort.\r\n\r\nOne question though: \r\nWouldn't the area to area collision code have the same issue? Wouldn't you need to add this sort there as well?\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4919909524/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4948975609","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-4948975609","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":4948975609,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJvtf-Q","user":{"login":"jice-dev","id":3774061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQwNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3774061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/jice-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-11T22:24:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T22:24:42Z","body":"> One question though: Wouldn't the area to area collision code have the same issue? Wouldn't you need to add this sort there as well?\r\n\r\nyes, sure, you're right\r\n\r\ni added this sort too in an additional commit","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4948975609/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5031761463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-5031761463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":5031761463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABK-qWNw","user":{"login":"jice-dev","id":3774061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQwNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3774061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/jice-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T08:26:00Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T08:26:00Z","body":"bump\r\ncould it be reviewed and merged if all is ok please ?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5031761463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5121200637","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-5121200637","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":5121200637,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMT9R_Q","user":{"login":"jice-dev","id":3774061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQwNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3774061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/jice-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T17:18:46Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T17:18:46Z","body":"bump","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5121200637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5240496167","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-5240496167","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":5240496167,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOFugJw","user":{"login":"jice-dev","id":3774061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQwNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3774061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/jice-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-10T12:48:23Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T12:48:23Z","body":"bump ? :)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5240496167/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5327451429","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-5327451429","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":5327451429,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPYp1JQ","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T11:22:43Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T16:31:21Z","body":"Since this only needs to differentiate two cases, partitioning would be more performant than sorting. Question is if going from O(n log n) to O(n) (and a lower constant factor) is worth the extra maintenance burden in this case.\r\n\r\nI'm inclined to say that sorting is not going to cause performance issues here but I thought I'd put the thought here anyways.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5327451429/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5335272379","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-5335272379","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":5335272379,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPgHLuw","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T23:05:48Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T04:55:13Z","body":"Beat me to it Skorpnok. The code shown below replaces the existing loop, and works for me if you want to change to partitioning (obviously with a similar piece of code for area).\r\n\r\nIf you used this sort of code @jice-dev, instead of the sort, then I would review and approve this. I know I am not a maintainer, but contributors can approve, and it can help maintainers make decisions. \r\n\r\nAlternatively I am happy to just make a new PR if you don't want to incorporate this.\r\n\r\nHowever, looking at the code revealed something far worse:\r\n\r\nHashMap is using the default allocator! Every single .remove is a default deallocation :|. We could consider using AHashMap (not sure). In any case, I replaced with a `PagedAllocator` locally, but that is not right either, because it can end up severely over-allocating in this case. The right tool for this job is to share a PagedAllocator across all Areas. \r\n\r\nHowever, that is for another PR or proposal or something.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n// The first pass issues `AREA_BODY_ADDED`, while the second pass issues `AREA_BODY_REMOVED`.\r\n// This execution order ensures that the callback doesn't incorrectly issue a body_exit signal.\r\nbool first_pass = true;\r\nfor (HashMap<BodyKey, BodyState , BodyKey>::Iterator next = monitored_bodies.begin(), E = next; E; E = next) {\r\n\t++next;\r\n\r\n\tif ((E->value.state > 0) || !first_pass) {\r\n\t\tres[0] = E->value.state > 0 ? PS2DE::AREA_BODY_ADDED : PS2DE::AREA_BODY_REMOVED;\r\n\t\tres[1] = E->key.rid;\r\n\t\tres[2] = E->key.instance_id;\r\n\t\tres[3] = E->key.body_shape;\r\n\t\tres[4] = E->key.area_shape;\r\n\r\n\t\tmonitored_bodies.remove(E);\r\n\r\n\t\tCallable::CallError ce;\r\n\t\tVariant ret;\r\n\t\tmonitor_callback.callp((const Variant **)resptr, 5, ret, ce);\r\n\r\n\t\tif (ce.error != Callable::CallError::CALL_OK) {\r\n\t\t\tERR_PRINT_ONCE(\"Error calling event callback method \" + Variant::get_callable_error_text(monitor_callback, (const Variant **)resptr, 5, ce));\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t} else if (E->value.state == 0) { // Nothing happened.\r\n\t\tmonitored_bodies.remove(E);\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tif (!next && first_pass) {\r\n\t\t// Start the second pass.\r\n\t\tfirst_pass = false;\r\n\t\tnext = monitored_bodies.begin();\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5335272379/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5339421667","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-5339421667","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":5339421667,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPkEb4w","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T08:18:01Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T08:18:01Z","body":"I just submitted an alternative PR #122581 to also fix the allocation thrashing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5339421667/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5547646144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120966#issuecomment-5547646144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120966","id":5547646144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSqpcwA","user":{"login":"jice-dev","id":3774061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NzQwNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3774061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/jice-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jice-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T23:32:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T23:32:33Z","body":"> I just submitted an alternative PR #122581 to also fix the allocation thrashing.\r\n\r\nok, so i close this one","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5547646144/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]